Modified by the devcroft authors. Every change is the single patch
devcroft-changes.patch, applied to the files it names:

- exec/shell channels can switch to a manual receive window, and the
  server returns credit through Handle::consumed only after the
  application has consumed the input;
- window adjustments add only newly received credit;
- sealed output queues behind a cancellation-safe partial-write cursor,
  with a soft application backpressure threshold and a reserve for
  control replies.

This fork exists only until the equivalent lands upstream.
